    "turn_text": "But we're still not there in terms of treating mental illness as an illness. I talk about this from time to time here, but my dad committed suicide when I was 19. And I didn't talk about it for 30 years because I thought somehow it would be Smurch him to talk about it. And I realized that's why he didn't go get help. And he was a mental health professional, but he didn't go get help because he thought it was a",
